# Cursor rules

This is a weisssrv cluster tenant repo. **Before making any change, read and
follow `.claude/skills/project-development/SKILL.md`** — the authoritative
workflow for this repo (also enforced by `.cursor/rules/project-development.mdc`,
`alwaysApply: true`). See [CLAUDE.md](CLAUDE.md) for the full guidance; it is the
canonical agent doc. Key rules:

- NEVER commit secrets — use `ExternalSecret` manifests referencing 1Password or
  GitLab CI/CD variables.
- NEVER push to `main` — branch → merge request, always.
- NEVER `kubectl apply` / `helm upgrade` to deploy — Flux owns Kubernetes state;
  preview with `kustomize build kubernetes/flux`, deploy by merging.
- Containers stay non-root with a read-only root filesystem; no `latest` tags.
- Run `task lint` before opening a merge request.
- Stay within your single namespace.
- CI comes in three shapes and this repo keeps one: `.gitlab-ci.yml` (shape
  `gitlab`, includes the shared `eric/weisssrv-lib` library at a pinned tag — do
  not re-inline it), `.github/workflows/` (shape `github`, a vendored
  equivalent), or neither (shape `none`, Flux-only). Check which is present
  before editing CI — see `docs/CI-SHAPES.md`.
- Scaffold with the `weisssrv-new-project` CLI; pick the CI shape with
  `./scripts/select-ci.sh` — see `docs/CONSUMING.md`.
